For your setup, don't run just the langfuse/langfuse container anymore. Langfuse v3 needs:

Plain Text
Langfuse
↓
PostgreSQL
↓
ClickHouse

The simplest way is Docker Compose.

Step 1: Create a folder
Shell
mkdir ~/langfuse-stack
 
cd ~/langfuse-stack
Step 2: Create docker-compose.yml
Shell
nano docker-compose.yml

services:

  postgres:
    image: postgres:16
    container_name: postgres
    restart: unless-stopped

    environment:
      POSTGRES_USER: langfuse
      POSTGRES_PASSWORD: langfuse123
      POSTGRES_DB: langfuse

    ports:
      - "5432:5432"

  clickhouse:
    image: clickhouse/clickhouse-server
    container_name: clickhouse
    restart: unless-stopped

    ports:
      - "8123:8123"
      - "9000:9000"

  langfuse:
    image: langfuse/langfuse
    container_name: langfuse

    restart: unless-stopped

    depends_on:
      - postgres
      - clickhouse

    ports:
      - "3000:3000"

    environment:

      DATABASE_URL: postgresql://langfuse:langfuse123@postgres:5432/langfuse

      CLICKHOUSE_URL: http://clickhouse:8123

=============

CLICKHOUSE_URL: http://clickhouse:8123

Save:

Plain Text
CTRL + O
ENTER
CTRL + X
Step 3: Start All Containers
Shell
docker compose up -d

Docker will pull:

Plain Text
postgres:16
clickhouse/clickhouse-server
langfuse/langfuse
Step 4: Verify
Shell
docker ps

Expected:

Plain Text
postgres Up
 
clickhouse Up
 
langfuse Up
Step 5: Check Logs
Shell
docker logs langfuse

You should no longer see:

Plain Text
DATABASE_URL is not configured

or

Plain Text
CLICKHOUSE_URL is not configured
Step 6: Open Langfuse

Inside Ubuntu:

Plain Text
http://localhost:3000

From Windows:

Find Ubuntu IP:

Shell
hostname -I
 

Example:

Plain Text
192.168.1.100

Open:

Plain Text
http://192.168.1.100:3000
If Existing Containers Exist

Remove old ones first:

Shell
docker rm -f langfuse
 
docker rm -f postgres

Then run:

Shell
docker compose up -d
 
Verify Architecture
Plain Text
Langfuse
↓
PostgreSQL
↓
ClickHouse

